hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17987","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, he said, Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from Malik ibn Sasaah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, While I was at the House, between asleep and awake, one of the three came to me between two men. I was brought a gold basin filled with wisdom and faith. I was cut from the throat to the pit of the belly. The heart was washed with Zamzam water, then filled with wisdom and faith. Then I was brought a mount below a mule and above a donkey. Then I set out with Jibril. We came to the lowest heaven. It was said, Who is this. He said, Jibril. It was said, Who is with you. He said, Muhammad. It was said, Has he been sent for. He said, Yes. It was said, Welcome to him, and excellent is the coming he has come. Then I came upon Adam, so I greeted him. So he said, Welcome to you as a son and a Prophet. Then we came to the second heaven. It was said, Who is this. It was said, Jibril. It was said, Who is with you. He said, Muhammad. The like of that. Then I came upon Yahya and Isa, so I greeted them. They said, Welcome to you as a brother and a Prophet. Then we came to the third heaven, the like of that. Then I came upon Yusuf, so I greeted him. So he said, Welcome to you as a brother and a Prophet. Then we came to the fourth heaven, the like of that. Then I came upon Idris, so I greeted him. So he said, Welcome to you as a brother and a Prophet. Then we came to the fifth heaven, the like of that. Then I came upon Harun, so I greeted him. So he said, Welcome to you as a brother and a Prophet. Then we came to the sixth heaven, the like of that. Then I came upon Musa, so I greeted him. So he said, Welcome to you as a brother and a Prophet. When I passed him he wept. It was said, What makes you weep. He said, O Lord, this boy whom You sent after me, more and finer of his nation will enter Paradise than will enter of my nation. Then we came to the seventh heaven, the like of that. Then I came upon Ibrahim, so I greeted him. So he said, Welcome to you as a son and a Prophet. He said, Then the Frequented House was raised to me. So I asked Jibril, and he said, This is the Frequented House; seventy thousand angels pray in it each day; when they leave it they never return to it, the last upon them. He said, Then the Lote Tree of the Utmost was raised to me, and its fruits were like the jars of Hajar, and its leaves like the ears of elephants, and at its root were four rivers, two hidden and two manifest. So I asked Jibril, and he said, As for the hidden two, they are in Paradise, and as for the manifest two, they are the Euphrates and the Nile. He said, Then fifty prayers were ordained for me. So I came upon Musa, and he said, What have you done. I said, Fifty prayers were ordained for me. So he said, I know people better than you; I treated the Children of Israel with the harshest treatment, and your nation will not bear that, so return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten for you. He said, So I returned to my Lord Almighty and asked Him to lighten for me, so He made them forty. Then I returned to Musa and came upon him. He said, What have you done. I said, He made them forty. So he said to me the like of his first saying. So I returned to my Lord Almighty, and He made them thirty. Then I came to Musa and informed him. So he said to me the like of his first saying. So I returned to my Lord Almighty, and He made them twenty, then ten, then five. Then I came upon Musa and informed him. So he said to me the like of his first saying. So I said, I am shy before my Lord Almighty from how many times I return to Him. So it was called out, I have enacted My obligation and lightened My servants, and I reward a good deed tenfold."
"17988","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us that Malik ibn Sasaah narrated to them that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, While I was at the Kabah, between asleep and awake, and he mentioned the hadith. He said, Then we set out to the seventh heaven. Jibril sought opening. It was said, Who is this. He said, Jibril. It was said, Who is with you. He said, Muhammad. It was said, Has he been sent for. He said, Yes. So it was opened for him. They said, Welcome to him, and excellent is the coming he has come. Then we came upon Ibrahim. I said, Who is this. Jibril said, This is your father Ibrahim, so greet him. So I greeted him. So he said, Welcome to the righteous son and the righteous Prophet. Then the Lote Tree of the Utmost was raised to me, and its leaves were like the ears of elephants, and its fruits like the jars of Hajar, and four rivers coming from its root, two manifest rivers and two hidden rivers. So I said, What is this, O Jibril. He said, As for the manifest two rivers, they are the Nile and the Euphrates, and as for the hidden two, they are two rivers in Paradise. He said, I was brought two vessels, one wine and the other milk. He said, So I took the milk. So Jibril said, You have hit the natural way."
"17989","Affan narrated to us, he said, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said, I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas ibn Malik that Malik ibn Sasaah narrated to him that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told them about the night he was taken. He said, While I was in al-Hatim, and once Qatadah said, in al-Hijr, reclining, a comer came to me and kept saying to his companion, the middle among the three. He said, So he came to me and split, and I heard Qatadah say, he cut, between this to this. Qatadah said, So I said to al-Jarud beside me, What does he mean. He said, From the hollow of his throat to his pubic hair, and I heard him say, from his chest to his pubic hair. He said, So my heart was extracted. I was brought a gold basin filled with faith and wisdom. My heart was washed, then stuffed, then returned. Then I was brought a mount below a mule and above a donkey, white. Al-Jarud said, It is al-Buraq, O Abu Hamzah. He said, Yes, its stride reaches its farthest sight. He said, So I was carried upon it. Jibril set out with me until he brought me to the lowest heaven. He sought opening. It was said, Who is this. He said, Jibril. It was said, Who is with you. He said, Muhammad. It was said, Has he been sent for. He said, Yes. It was said, Welcome to him, and excellent is the coming he has come. He said, So it was opened. When I passed through, there was Adam. So he said, This is your father Adam, so greet him. So I greeted him. He returned the greeting, then said, Welcome to the righteous son and the righteous Prophet. He said, Then he ascended until he came to the second heaven. He sought opening. It was said, Who is this. He said, Jibril. It was said, Who is with you. He said, Muhammad. It was said, Has he been sent for. He said, Yes. It was said, Welcome to him, and excellent is the coming he has come. He said, So it was opened. When I passed through, there were Yahya and Isa, and they are sons of maternal aunt. So he said, This is Yahya and Isa, so greet them. He said, So I greeted them. They returned the greeting, then said, Welcome to the righteous brother and the righteous Prophet. He said, Then he ascended until he came to the third heaven. He sought opening. It was said, Who is this. He said, Jibril. It was said, Who is with you. He said, Muhammad. Has he been sent for. He said, Yes. It was said, Welcome to him, and excellent is the coming he has come. He said, So it was opened. When I passed through, there was Yusuf. He said, This is Yusuf, so greet him. He said, So I greeted him. He returned the greeting and said, Welcome to the righteous brother and the righteous Prophet. Then he ascended until he came to the fourth heaven. He sought opening. It was said, Who is this. He said, Jibril. It was said, Who is with you. He said, Muhammad. It was said, Has he been sent for. He said, Yes. It was said, Welcome to him, and excellent is the coming he has come. He said, So it was opened. When I passed through, he said, There was Idris. He said, This is Idris, so greet him. He said, So I greeted him. He returned the greeting, then said, Welcome to the righteous brother and the righteous Prophet. He said, Then he ascended until he came to the fifth heaven. He sought opening. It was said, Who is this. He said, Jibril. It was said, Who is with you. He said, Muhammad. It was said, Has he been sent for. He said, Yes. It was said, Welcome to him, and excellent is the coming he has come. He said, So it was opened. When I passed through, there was Harun. He said, This is Harun, so greet him. He said, So I greeted him. He said, So he returned the greeting, then said, Welcome to the righteous brother and the righteous Prophet. He said, Then he ascended until he came to the sixth heaven. He sought opening. It was said, Who is this. He said, Jibril. It was said, Who is with you. He said, Muhammad. It was said, Has he been sent for. He said, Yes. It was said, Welcome to him, and excellent is the coming he has come. So it was opened. When I passed through, I was with Musa. He said, This is Musa, so greet him. So I greeted him. He returned the greeting, then said, Welcome to the righteous brother and the righteous Prophet. He said, When I passed beyond him he wept. It was said to him, What makes you weep. He said, I weep because a boy sent after me will have more of his nation enter Paradise than will enter it of my nation. He said, Then he ascended until he came to the seventh heaven. He sought opening. It was said, Who is this. He said, Jibril. It was said, Who is with you. He said, Muhammad. It was said, Has he been sent for. He said, Yes. It was said, Welcome to him, and excellent is the coming he has come. He said, So it was opened. When I passed through, there was Ibrahim. So he said, This is Ibrahim, so greet him. So I greeted him. He returned the greeting, then said, Welcome to the righteous son and the righteous Prophet. He said, Then the Lote Tree of the Utmost was raised to me, and its fruits were like the jars of Hajar, and its leaves like the ears of elephants. So he said, This is the Lote Tree of the Utmost. He said, And there were four rivers, two hidden and two manifest. So I said, What is this, O Jibril. He said, As for the hidden two, they are two rivers in Paradise, and as for the manifest two, they are the Nile and the Euphrates. He said, Then the Frequented House was raised to me. Qatadah said, And al-Hasan narrated to us from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he saw the Frequented House; seventy thousand angels enter it each day then never return to it. Then he returned to the hadith of Anas. He said, Then I was brought a vessel of wine, a vessel of milk, and a vessel of honey. He said, So I took the milk. He said, This is the natural way; you are upon it and your nation. He said, Then prayer was ordained, fifty prayers each day. He said, So I returned and passed Musa. So he said, What were you commanded. He said, I was commanded with fifty prayers each day. He said, Your nation cannot bear fifty prayers, and I have tried people before you and treated the Children of Israel with the harshest treatment, so return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten for your nation. He said, So I returned, and He removed ten from me. He said, So I returned to Musa. He said, What were you commanded. I said, Forty prayers each day. He said, Your nation cannot bear forty prayers each day, and I have tried people before you and treated the Children of Israel with the harshest treatment, so return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten for your nation. He said, So I returned, and He removed another ten from me. So I returned to Musa. He said to me, What were you commanded. I said, I was commanded with thirty prayers each day. He said, Your nation cannot bear thirty prayers each day, and I have tried people before you and treated the Children of Israel with the harshest treatment, so return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten for your nation. He said, So I returned, and He removed another ten from me. So I returned to Musa. He said to me, What were you commanded. I said, Twenty prayers each day. So he said, Your nation cannot bear twenty prayers each day, and I have tried people before you and treated the Children of Israel with the harshest treatment, so return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten for your nation. He said, So I returned, and I was commanded with ten prayers each day. So I returned to Musa. He said, What were you commanded. I said, Ten prayers each day. So he said, Your nation cannot bear ten prayers each day, for I have tried people before you and treated the Children of Israel with the harshest treatment, so return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten for your nation. He said, So I returned, and I was commanded with five prayers each day. So I returned to Musa. He said, What were you commanded. I said, I was commanded with five prayers each day. So he said, Your nation cannot bear five prayers each day, and I have tried people before you and treated the Children of Israel with the harshest treatment, so return to your Lord and ask Him to lighten for your nation. He said, I said, I have asked my Lord until I am shy before Him, but I am content and submit. When I passed through, a caller called, I have enacted My obligation and lightened My servants."
"17990","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah ibn Diamah, from Anas ibn Malik, from Malik ibn Sasaah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said, While I was at the Kabah, between asleep and awake, I heard a speaker say, one of the three, and he mentioned the hadith. He said, Then the Frequented House was raised for us; seventy thousand angels enter it each day; when they leave it they never return to it, the last upon them. He said, Then the Lote Tree of the Utmost was raised to me, and its leaves were like the ears of elephants, and he mentioned the hadith. He said, So I said, I went repeatedly to my Lord Almighty until I am shy. No, but I am content and submit. He said, When I passed beyond him I was called, I have lightened My servants, enacted My obligations, and made each good deed tenfold."
"17991","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said, Said informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, from Malik ibn Sasaah, a man of his people, and he mentioned it."
